6) Rotate Image(Rotate matrix by 90 degrees): ek 2D matrix ko 90 degree clockwise mein rotate karna hai

Brute Force Approach: indices ke hisab se logic banaye hai, ki rotate hone ke baad kya change ho raha hai indices mein , us behalf pe logic likhe hai

code:class Solution {
    public void rotate(int[][] matrix) {
        int rows = matrix.length;
        int cols = matrix[0].length;
        int[][] matrix1 = new int[rows][cols];
        for(int i=0;i<rows;i++)
        {
            for(int j=0;j<cols;j++)
            {
                matrix1[j][rows-i-1]=matrix[i][j];
            }
        }
        for(int i=0;i<rows;i++)
        {
            for(int j=0;j<cols;j++)
            {
                matrix[i][j]=matrix1[i][j];
            }
        }
    }
}

T.C. -> O(N^2)
S.C. -> O(N^2)

Optimal Approach: inplace karo , pehle transpose kar do uske baad saare rows ko reverse kardo

code: class Solution {
    public void rotate(int[][] matrix) {
        int n = matrix.length;
        for(int i=0;i<n;i++)
        {
            for(int j=i+1;j<n;j++)
            {
                int temp = matrix[i][j];
                matrix[i][j] = matrix[j][i];
                matrix[j][i] = temp;
            }
        }
        for(int i=0;i<n;i++)
        {
            int left = 0 , right = n-1;
            while(left<right)
            {
                int temp = matrix[i][left];
                matrix[i][left] = matrix[i][right];
                matrix[i][right] = temp;
                left++;
                right--;
            }
        }
    }
}

T.C. ->   O(N^2)     

7) Find the Duplicate Number

Brute Force Approach: Sort the given array then the duplicates number will be together and then the value of i will be equal to i+1

T.C. -> O(N Log N) 
S.C. -> O(1)

improved version of this: ek frequency array banayenge , with all zeores and check karke mark karte jayenge us number ke index pe 1 aur woh , jab dobara aayega tab 1 already marked hai , pata chal jayega ki duplicate hai

T.C. -> O(N)
S.C. -> O(N)

we improved T.C. but S.C. badh gaya.

Most Optimal Sol: most optimal sol uses the linked list cycle method 

code: class Solution {
    public int findDuplicate(int[] nums) {
        int slow = nums[0];
        int fast = nums[0];
        do{
            slow = nums[slow];
            fast = nums[nums[fast]];
        } while(slow!=fast);
        fast = nums[0];
        while(slow!=fast){
            slow = nums[slow];
            fast = nums[fast];
        }
        return slow;
    }
}


🔹 Step 1: Cycle kyun bana?

👉 Kyuki duplicate hai, isliye path circular ho gaya

🔹 Step 2: Fast catches slow
Fast 2 step lega
Slow 1 step lega

